   "edited": false
  },
  "14": {
   "text": "quently as the men. In",
   "edited": false
  },
  "15": {
   "text": "the Pacific villages the",
   "edited": false
  },
  "16": {
   "text": "Chukchee and the Eskimo",
   "edited": false
  },
  "17": {
   "text": "young women also have",
   "edited": false
  },
  "18": {
   "text": "overcoats made of thin",
   "edited": false
  },
  "19": {
   "text": "guts of seal and walrus",
   "edited": false
  },
  "20": {
   "text": "carefully bleached and",
   "edited": false
  },
  "21": {
   "text": "quite transparent. They",
   "edited": false
  },
  "22": {
   "text": "are exceedingly light, and",
   "edited": false
  },
  "23": {
   "text": "not ungraceful in appear-",
   "edited": false
  },
  "24": {
   "text": "ance (Fig. 180). The",
   "edited": false
  },
  "25": {
   "text": "guts are neatly stitched",
   "edited": false
  },
  "26": {
   "text": "together in long bands,",
   "edited": false
  },
  "27": {
   "text": "and the coat is trimmed",
   "edited": false
  },
  "28": {
   "text": "with tassels and small red",
   "edited": false
  },
  "29": {
   "text": "tufts of feathers from the",
   "edited": false
  },
  "30": {
   "text": "heads of crested auks.",
   "edited": false
  },
  "31": {
   "text": "It is probable that this",
   "edited": false
  },
  "32": {
   "text": "frock or coat belonged",
   "edited": false
  },
  "33": {
   "text": "originally to the Eskimo",
